Develop a JavaScript program that can evaluate the geometric mean of an array composed of at least four integers. Take into account that the array needs to be a dynamically sized one built from user input. To increase difficulty, provide a piece of code as a reference containing errors for the candidate to identify, troubleshoot, and fix.

#Reference Code#:

```
function geometricMean(arr) {
    var product = 1;
    for (var i = 0; i < arr.lenght; i++) {
        product *= arr[i];
    }
    return Math.pow(product, 4 / arr.length);
}

console.log(geometricMean([7, 2, 4, 12]));
```

Note: Be sure to run your function through validating and handling any possible erroneous input. For example, your program should properly respond to non-integer, negative, and 0 values.

Create an interwoven string with alternating characters from two given strings, handling edge cases when one input string is longer than the other. As an additional challenge, identify and handle an error in the given example code snippet.

Example strings:
string str1 = "HELLO";
string str2 = "WORLD";

Erroneous code snippet:
```cpp
string interwovenStr;
for (int i = 0; i < str1.length() && i < str2.length(); ++i) {
    interwovenStr += str1[i];
    interwovenStr += str2[i];
}
```

Remember to account for instances when the lengths of the input strings are not equal.
